{
  "id": "ts_world_ground",
  "kind": "object",
  "type": "tileset",
  "name": "Menu map ground tiles",
  "notes": "Every 8x8 tile of the menu map's ground layer (layer 2): the Green Meadow's grass, garden bed and cave earth (in pal_menu_field) and, for each of the 8 lands, its world's plain ground and small things and the 15 pieces of its obstacle (lava, water, cliffs, ravines, bog, open sky, jungle, haunted hedge) laid on a dual grid: a piece comes from which of its 4 corners are inside the obstacle, so edges, outer and inner corners join up. Each land's tiles are drawn in that world's own ground palette (the tile's 'palette' index into 'palettes', 1 = the Canyon's ... 8 = the Hollow's). None is solid: the collision layer (map_world_solid) holds the invisible solid tile wherever a wall is.",
